      "englishText": "Avadhānī: (begins with a stuti to Lord Vishnu)\n\nO Lord, I make salutations to Thee, the glorious Being. Thou hast entered into me through Thy intelligent power and roused the dormant faculty of my speech. Being the Lord of all powers, Thou kindlest to activity all other organs of my mind.\n\n(Now the 1st round of the Avadhāna begins)\n\nNiṣiddhākṣarī: Please compose a verse of prayer to Sri Aurobindo in the Anustubh metre. \n\n(The Avadhānī replies to the Niṣiddhākṣarī's request with one syllable forming the beginning of a word. The Niṣiddhākṣarī tries to guess the next syllable and prohibits that syllable. This process continues till the completion of the shloka.)\n\nAvadhānī: 'A'\n\nNiṣiddhākṣarī: 'Ra' is prohibited' (the Niṣiddhākṣarī anticipates the word 'Aravinda' and prohibits 'ra' so as to prevent the Avadhānī from composing the word 'Aravinda'.)\n\nAvadhānī: (gives the next letter) 'ma'\n\nAprastutaprasanga: (with a view to disturb his concentration asks the Avadhānī) O great Avadhānī, when I was listening to your poem, which you recited a few minutes back, I remembered Sarasvatabhadra, a character in the drama Padmapravrittika written by Shudraka. Just like you, he used to search for new words to write poetry. Another character (in the drama) asked him: 'O you cobbler, who splits words and joins them in order to compose new words, how is it that you search for new words like the cowherd boy who, being lost in the forest, searches for the fresh footprints of his animals to find the way out.' O great Avadhānī, are you like that cobbler?",
      "sanskritDevanagari": "अवधानी:   योऽन्तः प्रविश्य मम वाचमिमां प्रसुप्ताम्\n            सञ्जीवयत्यखिलशक्तिधरः स्वधाम्ना । ।\n            अन्यांश्च हस्तचरणश्रवणत्वगादीन्\n            प्राणान् नमो भगवते पुरुषाय तुभ्यम् ॥\n\nनिषिद्धाक्षरी:  सम्प्रति अरविन्दमहर्षीणां प्रार्थनम् एकेन श्लोकेन अनुष्टुप् छन्दसि पृच्छामि ।\n\nअवधानी: अ\n\nनिषिद्धाक्षरी:  रेफः निषिद्धः । र निषिद्धः । \n\nअवधानी: म\n\nअप्रस्तुतप्रसङ्गः:  अवधानिवर्य ! भवतः इदानीं तत्र कविताश्रवणसमये मम एकः सन्दर्भः स्मृतिपथमागच्छत् ।  शुद्रकः  पप्रव`Ùाकभाणम् अरचयत् किल ?  तत्र सारस्वतभद्रः इति कश्चित् भवादृशः सः एवमेव कवितां  कुर्वन् पदानि अन्वेषति । तदा तत्र नटः समागत्य पृच्छति— “भोः पुराणपदच्छेदग्रथनचर्मकार ! किं नष्टगोपाल इव नवपदानि अन्वेषसे ?”  किं भवन्तः अपि तादृशाः ?"
