      "englishText": "Aprastutaprasanga: (jokingly says) Having seen your state of being and the condition of your body, he is afraid that when he hits the bell strongly, whether you will\n\nAvadhānī: ...stay here or not?\n\nAprastutaprasanga: Yes, exactly.\n\nCommentator: He is also like you.\n\nAvadhānī: But being surrounded by eight gigantic elephants (the questioners), where can I go? Do strike hard! Strike hard! \n\nAvadhānī: (taking up the previous request of the Niṣiddhākṣarī gives the next syllable): 'ma'\n\nAprastutaprasanga: (interferes once again): O Avadhānī, do you like watching the television? Nowadays there are many channels, like Zee-channel, V-channel or E-channel, which one can watch on the TV. One can watch\n\nprogrammes that are quite entertaining. My question is, after seeing this drama or that programme, is it still possible to engage in the effort of concentration which the task of Avadhana demands? \n\nAvadhānī: Surely. I am in the midst of all these channels (cānāla madhye). (Playing with the word 'cānāla, which is adapted from the English 'channel', he continues) For I am in 'the midst of fire' (cha-anala-madhye), so it seems to me. When I am in the midst of channels, I am truly in the midst of fire — that's what I feel. But I am also without channels, not involved in them (vicānāla), and I wish to be without movement (vicalanam). For being vichanala, not involved in any channel, I am truly non-moving. I feel myself stationed in solitude. \n\nAprastutaprasanga: (playing again with the word 'vicānāla') It appears to me that you are more interested in the V-Channel.",
