      "englishText": "Samasyā2 :  bhagnāpyabhagnā mama puṣpamālā\n\n(My garland of flowers — broken yet not broken)\n(The metre used by the Samasyā is Indravajrā.The Avadhānī too must compose his shloka in the same metre)\n\nThe Bell: (rings for the 3rd time)\n\nAprastutaprasanga: O dear Avadhānī, are you capable of weaving a garland? Have you ever practiced at home?\n\nAvadhānī: You mean making flower garlands? If I don't have anything to do, I\n\nmake garlands of flowery words.3 Sometimes I also prepare a flower garland made of flowers of devotion and offer it to God in the form of a poetic composition.\n\nAprastutaprasanga: But now your task is to mend a broken garland.\n\nAvadhānī: Yes, I will mend the flower garland of a broken heart with the help of a proper understanding.\n\nVyastākṣarī: I have a shloka in my mind, in which the fifth syllable is 'ma'.\n\n2Samasya, 'problem', from root 'as' and suffix 'sam', means 'to put together', 'to be made entire'. Thus a part of a verse to be completed. \n 3The Avadhānī is a passionate poet too.",
      "sanskritDevanagari": "समस्या:  भग्नाप्यभग्ना मम पुष्पमाला।\n\nअवधानी:  भग्नाप्यभग्ना------- \n\nसमस्या:  मम पुष्पमाला ।                                                                    🔔 (घण्टा ३)\n\nअप्रस्तुतप्रसङ्गः:  किं भोः अवधानिवर्य!ः भवन्तः पुष्पमालाग्रथनेऽपि समथर्ाः वा ।   किञ्चद् अभ्यासः अस्ति ग`हे ?\n\nअवधानी:  पुष्पमालाग्रथने----?  ;दि अहं किमपि का;± न करोमि तदा अहं पदपुष्पमालां करोमि ।   कदाचित्  भक्ितपुष्पमालां भगवते समर्पयामि] रचयत्वैव ।\n\nअप्रस्तुतप्रसङ्गः:  परन्तु भगëमायासंयोजनं तु अधुनैव\n\nअवधानी:  भग्नमनः पुष्पमालाम् अभगëां करोमि हितबोधेन ।\n\nव्यस्ताक्षरी:  कËत् श्लोकः ।  तस्; पञ्चममक्षरं म"
