      "englishText": "(Now it is the turn of the Varṇanā questioner.)\n\nVarṇanā: In this assembly we find a variegated audience, — there are the lovers of Sanskrit, there are the questioners, and there are all those who are in same way devoted and working for Sanskrit. Please compose a poem in Mālinī metre on this topic.\n\nAvadhānī: Do you want me to describe this assembly?\n\nVarṇanā: Yes, right.\n\nAprastutaprasanga: Should he compose in Malini6, or in Manini7? I believe, he knows the ways of Manini well.\n\nAvadhānī: No, Māninī is not necessary. I already have a Māninī (meaning his wife at home).\n\nVarṇanā: Since the respected Avadhānī has  come to this place (alone), so she has become a Māninī8.\n\nCommentator: That means she is angry.\n(The Avadhānī completes then the first quarter of the Varṇanā-item):\n\nThe Bell: (sounds here for the 5th time)\n\nAvadhānī: mahitavividhabhāṣāsatkriyābhūṣitāṅgaḥ\n\n(The honoured who are assembled here speak different languages;\ntrue conduct are their ornaments)\n\nPresident: (sums up): The Avadhānī was asked by the questioners to compose a verse in Mālinī metre, describing this assembly. Here he has completed the first quarter.\n\n6A metre of fifteen syllables.\n 7'Manini' means woman. Metre in Sanskrit is called 'vritta' which also means 'the way'. \n 8Here Manini is used in the sense of a dejected lady.",
      "sanskritDevanagari": "वर्णना  अत्रा सभायां विविधप्रकारकाः सामाजिकाः  समसेवकाË प`च्छकाः सन्ित ।  एतानध्िाव`ðत्;] सभामध्िाव`ðत्; मायिनीव`Ùो किमपि प|म् ।\n\nअवधानी:  सभास्थानम् ?\n\nवर्णना  आम् सभास्थानम् ।\n\nअप्रस्तुतप्रसङ्गः:  किं भोः मायिनी वा मानिनी वा ?  एते तु मानिनीव`Ùां सम्यक् जानन्ित ।\n\nअवधानी: मानिनी नावश्;की ।   एका मानिनी अस्ति मम ।\n\nवर्णना  अवधानी:महाशयः अत्रा आगतः इति सा मानिनी जाता\n\nव्याख्याकारः:  वुðपिता जाता इत्यथ्र्ाः                                                               🔔 (घण्टा ५)\n\nअवधानी: महितविविधभाषा सत्क्रियाभूषिताङ्गाः\n\nसभापतिः:  व.र्ाने मायिनीव`Ùो इयं सभा व.र्ानीया इति प`च्छवैðः प`Îम् ।   तत्र अवधानिना प्रथमः पादः उक्तः ।  महितविविधभाषा सत्क्रियाभूषिताङ्गाः ।"
