      "englishText": "(The 2nd round of the Avadhāna)\n\nAvadhānī: (Shall I start) with Nishedha9?\n\nNiṣiddhākṣarī: No, not with Nishedha. Nishedha can not be applied to the first syllable. \n\nCommentator: What! you want to have prohibition in the first syllable itself?\n\nAvadhānī: We have accepted the job. Rest is his wish.\n\nAprastutaprasanga: O Sir, when you speak of 'job', I just remember that you are a principal (pramshupala). How a person of a short height like you, can be a prāṃśu-pāla?\n\nAvadhānī: I am not a 'prāṃśu-pāla'10, a ruler of the tall. For 'prāṃśu' means 'one who has excellent rays'11 My name is Prabhakar12, that's why I am a guardian of light—'prāṃśu' and 'pāla' together mean 'prāṃśupāla', guardian of excellent rays. But here, 'pālaḥ' also means 'one whose name is adorned by the letter pa' (as in Prabhākara). In fact, governed or controlled by the rays or ' who has excellent rays which rule everything'. So, all the meanings apply to me. Sugriva says in the Rāmāyaṇa, 'No one is greater than me'. In the same way there is none greater than me in my school.\n\nVyastākṣarī: The eighth syllable is 'ra'.\n\n9Relating to the activity of the Niṣiddhākṣarī, who prohibits syllables. \n10Here the Avadhānī uses the literal Sanskrit meaning, i.e. 'pramshu' = tall, 'pala' = ruler; \n'pramshupala' = ruler of the tall.\n11This time 'pramshu' is split into the two words 'pra' and 'amshu', meaning, 'one with excellent rays'. \nThe large number of possible meanings for one word is typical of the Sanskrit language and allows with ease for much wordplays. \n12Giver of light (prabha), an epithet of Lord Surya or the Sun.",
      "sanskritDevanagari": "अवधानी:  निषेधपूर्वकम् ।\n\nनिषिद्धाक्षरी:  न निषेधपूर्वकं निषेधः नास्ति ।  अयं निषेधप्रव`Ùाः प्रथमाक्षरे अस्ति ।\n\nव्याख्याकारः:  किं प्रथमाक्षरेऽपि निषेधमिच्छन्ित भवन्तः !\n\nअवधानी:  व;मत्रा दायत्वं स्वीव`ðतवन्तः ।  तेषामिÎम् ।\n\nअप्रस्तुतप्रसङ्गः:  भोः दायत्वमित्;ुक्ते मया स्मर्यते भवन्तः प्रांशुपायाः इति मया Jुतमिदानीम् । कथं åस्वः प्रांशुपायः जातः इति ।\n\nअवधानी: अहं प्रांशुनां पायकः न ।  प्रांशुः प्रव`ðÎाः अंशवः ;स्; सन्ित सः प्रांशुः ।  अहं प्रभाकरः नामëा ।     अतःप्रांशुËासौ पायË ।  प  पकारेण अयति शोभते इति पायः ।  वस्तुतः प्रांशुविधेयः ।  प्रांशवः   पायाः  ;स्; सन्ित सोऽहं प्रांशुपायः ।  सवर्ेऽपि मÙाः---रामा;णे अस्ति मÙाः प्रत्;मरः कËत् नास्तिसुग्रीवस्; उक्ितः इति ।  अतः अस्माकं कयाशायायामपि मÙाः प्रत्;मरः कËत् नास्ति ।\n\nव्यस्ताक्षरी:  आर्यषष्ठमक्षरं र"
