      "englishText": "Niṣiddhākṣarī: Please compose the second quarter of the (Niṣiddhākṣarī)— item.\n\nBell: (sounds for the 8th time) \n\nAvadhānī: (starting the pāda): 'bhu'\n\nNiṣiddhākṣarī: 'va' is forbidden.(anticipating the word 'bhuva' meaning earth).\n\nAvadhānī: 'na'\n\nNiṣiddhākṣarī: Please give another syllable! (unable to guess the word the Avadhānī has in his mind)\n\nAvadhānī: 'ye' \n\nNiṣiddhākṣarī: So the verse starts 'bhyudaye';\n I forbid 'ta'. (anticipating the word the word 'tasmin' meaning 'in him or that' or 'tathā' meaning 'like that').\n\nAvadhānī: 'na' (completing the word 'bhūdayena' meaning by the king of the earth).\n\nNiṣiddhākṣarī: Please give one more syllable (as a new word is starting).\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 9th time)\nAvadhānī: 'ma'\n\nNiṣiddhākṣarī: 'ha' is forbidden. (anticipating the word 'mahā' meaning great).\n\nVyastākṣarī: The 15th syllable is 'na'.\n\nAvadhānī: 'na'\n\nAprastutaprasanga: (interrupting), O Avadhānī, yesterday, on the way to Pondicherry we passed a place called Tindivanam.\n\nAvadhānī: (catching the suggestion intended by the Aprastutaprasanga) Do you mean the Telugu Tindivanam13?'\n\n13'Tindivanam' in Telugu means 'where food is available in plenty'. \nThe suggestion is easily understood, as many of the participants are from Andhra, where Telugu is spoken.",
      "sanskritDevanagari": "निषिद्धाक्षरी:  निषिधाक्षया± }तीयः पादः ।\n \n(घण्टा 8)\n\nअवधानी:  भु                  \n\nनिषिद्धाक्षरी:  वकारः निषिद्धः । \n\nअवधानी:  ना\n\nनिषिद्धाक्षरी:  अन्यः कËदक्षरम् \n\nअवधानी:  ये\n\nनिषिद्धाक्षरी:  भुनाये !!  तकारः निषिद्धः\n\nअवधानी:  न\n\nनिषिद्धाक्षरी:  दी;तामन्यः                 (घण्टा 9)\n\nअवधानी: म\n\nनिषिद्धाक्षरी:  हकारः निषिद्धः\n\nव्यस्ताक्षरी:  पञ्चदशमक्षरं न\n\nअवधानी:  न\n\nअप्रस्तुतप्रसङ्गः:  भोः  अवधानिवर्य!  áः  ;दा अहं  पाण्डिच्चेरीमागच्छन्  आसम्  तत्र  मध्ये  तिण्डिवनम्  इति एकमागतम् ।\n\nअवधानी:  तेयुगु तिण्डिवनं वा ?"
