      "englishText": "Aprastutaprasanga: Yes, exactly. That time I was very hungry. So I wanted to have something to eat. Yet nothing eatable (tindi) could be found. Why was it so,— can you explain? \n\nAvadhānī: (to the audience): He saw Tindivanam. 'Tindi' in Telugu means food and 'vanam' means rich, good. The Aprastutaprasanga thought that this was a place where one could find good food. But 'vanam' means forest (in Sanskrit). So, actually that was a forest for eatable things meaning no food was available. By mistake he has gone to Tindivanam. (Turning to the Aprastutaprasanga) Really, you made a mistake by going to Tindivanam.\n\nNiṣiddhākṣarī:\t(expecting the word 'mahā'): 'ha' is forbidden.\n\nAvadhānī: 'nah'\n\nVyastākṣarī: the fourth syllable is 'na'.\n\nAvadhānī: Understood, 'na'.\n\nVyastākṣarī: The seventh syllable is 'mam'.\n(The Avadhānī repeats the same).\n\nNiṣiddhākṣarī: 'ka' is forbidden (anticipating the word 'manaskama' meaning desired by the mind)\n\nAvadhānī: 'sthi'\n\nNiṣiddhākṣarī: 'ta' is forbidden (expecting the word 'sthita' meaning stationed)\n\nAvadhānī: 'ram'. (Now the complete pāda of the Niṣiddhākṣarī reads):\n\nPresident: The second pāda of the Niṣiddhākṣarī is herewith completed.\n\nAvadhānī: (takes up next the second line of Samasyā and completes it in one stretch):\n\nbhātāpyabhātā prabalāśrunetre\n\n(It seems to appear and disappear in front of my eyes, full of tears)\n\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 10th time)\n\nVyastākṣarī: The eighth syllable is 'va'\t\n\nAvadhānī: 'va'\n\nAprastutaprasanga: O great Avadhānī, Kalidasa tells us that 'All that is old (purana)is not gold'. Which Purāṇa does he mean?14\n\nAvadhānī: He means the Navapurāna15, where it is discussed what is new and what is old, whether the new should be accepted or the old.\n\nVyastākṣarī: The first syllable is 'a'.\n\nAvadhānī: So it is 'a' (akāra)! In the Sanskrit alphabet the first syllable is 'a'.\n(Avadhānī continues immediately to complete the second line of the Dattapadī using the word 'ratna')\n\t\nratnāḍhyam bhavadiyabhavyamukutam dūrāt kshanam sevyate\n(The beautiful crown on your head is enjoyed by us from afar)\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 11th time)\n\n14The word 'purana' can be used in the double sense of 1) the literal sense 'old', 2) indicating the scriptures called 'Puranas'.\n15Literaly, 'new purana'. Kalidasa has used the word 'purana' here in the primary sense of 'old'. He didn't refer to any Purana in his words. 'Navapurana' is a word coined by the Avadhani, meaning 'New Purana'. It does not exist among the scriptures known as Puranas. The Avadhani here plays on the suggestion thrown up by the questioner by combining both implicatios in his answer.",
      "sanskritDevanagari": "अप्रस्तुतप्रसङ्गः:  आम् तदेव ।  तदा मम बुभुक्षा महती आसीत् ।  तस्मात् तत्र किमपि तत्र यभ्;ते वा इदानीमिष्टम् । परन्तु न किञ्चत् तिण्डि यब्धं तत्र ।   त£ह किं स्यात् तत् ?\n\nअवधानी:   तत्र तैः तिण्डिवनं द`ष्टम् ।   तिण्डि इत्युक्ते तेयुगुभाषायां भोजनम् ।  भोजनस्; वनं नाम सम`)ं    भोजनं भवति इति मतम् महाशयेन ।   किन्तु वनमिति शब्दस्; अर.;मित्;थ्र्ाः ।   अतः भोजनस्; अर.यं तत् ।  ति.डोः वनं तिण्डिवनम् । अतः भोजनस्; अर.यास्थानम् ।  न यभ्;ते इत्यथ्र्ाः।    अतः भ्रान्त्या तिण्डिवनं गतम् ।   भ्रान्त्या तिण्डिवनं गतं प्रभवता ।\n\nनिषिद्धाक्षरी:   हकारः निषिद्धः\n\nअवधानी:   नः\n\nव्यस्ताक्षरी:  चतुथ्र्ामक्षरं ण\n\nअवधानी:  चतुथ्र्ामक्षरं ण\n\nव्यस्ताक्षरी:  सप्तममक्षरं मम्\n\nअवधानी:  सप्तममक्षरं मम्\n\nनिषिद्धाक्षरी:  ककारः निषिद्धः\n\nअवधानी:  स्थ\n\nनिषिद्धाक्षरी:  तकारः निषिद्धः\n\nअवधानी:  रम्\n\nसभापतिः:  निषिधाक्षया± }तीयः पादः अवसितः\n\nसमस्या:यां }तीयः पादः\n\nअवधानी:  भाताप्यभाता प्रबलाश्रुनेत्रे     (घण्टा 10)\n\nव्यस्ताक्षरी:  अष्टममक्षरं वा\n\nअवधानी:  व\n\nअप्रस्तुतप्रसङ्गः:  भोः अवधानिवर्य! कायिदासः कथ;ति पुराणमित्येव न साधु सर्वमिति  ।   किं पुराणमनंय{; अयं कथ;ति ?  \n\nअवधानी:  पुराणमित्येव न साधु सर्वमिति वदन्ित  किं पुराणम् ।  नवपुराणम्] इत्युक्ते नवपुराणम् अध्िाव`ðत्;   तत्र किं नवं किं पुराणम् इति नव इत्यस्; पुराण प्रचयति ।  नवं स्वीकरणीयं वा पुराणं स्वीकरणीयं वा इति ।\n\nव्यस्ताक्षरी:  प्रथममक्षरम् अ\n\nदत्तपद्याम् }तीयः पादः ।\n\nअवधानी: अकारम् ।  अकारः प्रथमाक्षरम् ।                                                    (घण्टा 11)     \nरत्नाढîं भवदीयभव्यमुकुटं दूरात् क्षणं संद`शं ।\nरत्नाढîं भवदीयभव्यमुकुटं दूरात् क्षणं सेव्यते । \nरत्नाढîं भवदीयभव्यमुकुटं दूरात् क्षणं सेव्यते ।"
