      "englishText": "Vyastākṣarī: The ninth syllable is 'ja'.\n\nAvadhānī: 'ja'.\n\nPresident: Please compose the second line of the varṇanā.\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 12th time)\n\nAvadhānī: ruciralalitayogaprakriyā \n(the very enjoyable activity of yoga)\n\nAprastutaprasanga: O Avadhānī, when hearing 'prakriyā' (process, activity), it came to my mind, that nowadays computers have entered everywhere...\n\nAvadhānī: (repeats the second line of the\n\nVarṇanā by adding 'śuddhabhāvāḥ', so the whole second line reads:) \n\nruciralalitayogaprakriyāśuddhabhāvāḥ\n(having acquired purity of nature by the enjoyable and beautiful  process of yoga) \n\nAprastutaprasanga:\t(starts again:) Computers have now a days entered everywhere. They can be used for different purposes. By introducing computers unemployment has increased, — people become idle. Some even say that in future there will be no more scholars, because the computers will do everything. Is this true?\t\n\nPresident: Then there will be no more need of Avadhānīs.",
