      "englishText": "Aprastutaprasanga:\tIn future the computers will do the work of the Avadhānīs and, (pointing to the Avadhānī) then your ... \n\nAvadhānī: importance will not be there. Computers have been devised by us. But first God implanted the computer into our intelligence. And there was no unemployment problem, even when there were crores of computers (here the Avadhānī refers to the human minds). So how can there be an unemployment problem now with these small computers. People will not be idle because, when everyone has a computer, they will still go on fighting or exercising with the computers. So there is nothing to be worried about that people will sit lazily at home.\n\nAprastutaprasanga: But there will be the Virus problem everywhere.\n\nVyastākṣarī: The thirteenth syllable is 'tha'.\n\nAvadhānī: Ok, the thirteenth syllable is 'tha'",
