      "englishText": "Vyastākṣarī: The tenth syllable is 'gad'.\n\nAvadhānī: 'gad'.\n\nVyastākṣarī: Sir the second syllable is 'ra'.\n\nThe Bell: (sounds for the14th time)\n\nCommentator: One question came to my mind while sitting here, in this assembly. Shall I ask? You (the Avadhānī) told the audience that you are a bird and for that you used the word 'vihaṅgamikā', which is in feminine gender. Now I have a doubt, whether you are a man or a woman.\n\nAvadhānī: Who I am truly will be known at the end of this programme. But let me tell you, that you are also feminine in nature. I am of feminine nature, as well as she, as well as he over there. For everyone is in reality   (a woman) Prakriti.\n\nPresident:\t(explains) The whole world consists of these two (principles) — masculine and feminine: The Lord alone is the Supreme Person, the Supreme Man. Everything else, around Him — is of feminine Nature.17\n\nVyastākṣarī: Sir, the fourteenth syllable is 'va'.\n\n17The reference here is made to the ancient Sankhya philosophy, who envisioned one Supreme Being and Conscious Principle, Purusha, while all else, the outer world, is a creation of Prakriti, which exists yet for His Pleasure. The reference is also to the symbolism of Sri Krishna's play with the Gopis as propounded in the Vaishnava system; where Krishna is the only Purusha, while all human beings are souls as Gopis aspiring for Krishna.",
      "sanskritDevanagari": "व्यस्ताक्षरी:  दशममक्षरं गद् \n\nअवधानी:  दशममक्षरं गद्\n\nव्यस्ताक्षरी:  आर्य }ती;मक्षरं रा                                                             (घण्टा 14)\n\nव्याख्याकारः:  सभ्येऽस्मन्  मम एकः प्रश्नः \nवर्तते ।  अपि प`च्छाामि ?\nअहं काचन विहङ्गमिका इत्युक्तं मम संशयः जातः भवान् पुमान् वा ýी वा ?\n\nअवधानी:  वस्तुतः कः इति सभान्ते निणर्ेतल्;म् ।  भवती अपि ýी ।  अहमपि ýी ।  सापि ýी ।  एषा सवर्ापि प्रव`ðतिरेव ।\n\nसभापतिः:  ýीप्रा;मितरं जगत् ।  भगवतः सêाधौ भगवान् एवैðव परमपु#षः ।  भगवतः सêाधौ अन्यत् सव± ýीप्रायः ।\n\nव्यस्ताक्षरी:  आर्य चतुर्दशमक्षरं व"
