      "englishText": "(The 3rd and 4th round of Avadhāna)\n\n(Here, as there was a shortage of time the President asked the Avadhānī to complete the 3rd and 4th pādas of all the incomplete stanzas.):\n\t\nAvadhānī: (Avadhānī composes the third and fourth pāda of the Niṣiddhākṣarī-shloka)    \n\nkritye kuśalatābrahma\nrupitam yena te namah\n\n(To Thee, who hast established the Brahman of perfection in works, to Thee my obeisance)\n\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 15th time.)\n\nPresident: Herewith the task given by the Niṣiddhākṣarī is completed.\n\nAprastutaprasanga: To whom is the obeisance given?\n\nAvadhānī: To him who is behind us\n\n(pointing to Sri Aurobindo's photo)\n\nVyastākṣarī: The third syllable is 'va'.\n\nAvadhānī. 'va'\n\nPresident: Now the third pāda of the Samasyā should be composed.\n\nThe Bell: ( sounds for the 16th time)\n\nAvadhānī: kanthe'pyakanthe virahe priyā me\n\n(and he adds to it the fourth line which \nhad been originally given by the \nSamasyā-questioner)\n\nbhagnāpyabhagnā mama puṣpamālā\n\n(It is around my neck and yet it is'nt, \nin the absence of the beloved ,\nIt is broken, and yet it is \nunbroken, my garland \nof flowers!)",
      "sanskritDevanagari": "निषिधाक्षया± त`ती;-चतुथ्र्ापादौ\n\nअवधानी:  व`ðत्ये--- (घण्टा 15) \nवुðशयता ब्रà (सभापतिः:- त`तीयः पदः पू.र्ाः) :पितं येन ते नमः               \n \nसभापतिः:  निषिद्धाक्षरी: श्लोकः सम्पू.र्ाः ।\n\nअपस्तुतप्रसङ्गः  कस्मै अयं नमस्कारः ?\n\nअवधानी:  यः प`ष्ठतः अस्ति\n\nव्यस्ताक्षरी:  त`ती;मक्षरं व\n\nअवधानी:  त`ती;मक्षरं व\n\nसभापतिः:  समस्या:यां त`तीयः पादः                                                             (घण्टा 16)\n\nअवधानी:  क.ठेऽप्;क.ठे विरहे प्रिया मे\n           क.ठेऽप्;क.ठे विरहे प्रिया मे\n           भग्नाप्यभग्ना मम पुष्पमाला ।।"
