      "englishText": "President: The Samasyā has been completed. Now the third and fourth line of the Dattapadī-item is to be composed.\n \nAvadhānī: nūtanāviṣkṛtikāriṇī surucirā divyajjaganmaṅgalā\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 17th time).\n\nAvadhānī: pratnā te shubhamurtiradya hridaye dhāryā    vṛṣādrīśvara \n(Discoverer of new things, beautiful, \nheavenly, ancient, auspicious on earth, \nis Thy shining image. May we hold it today \nin our  heart chamber, O Vrishadrishvara !)\n\nPresident: The four quarters of the Dattapadī-item are herewith completed. Now the third and fourth pāda of the Varṇanā are to be taken up.\n\nVyastākṣarī: The twelfth syllable is 'ksha'.\n\nAvadhānī: 'ksha'.\n\nAprastutaprasanga: Revered Avadhānī, in your\n\nverse you have worshipped Lord Vṛṣādrīśvara, \nor was it Goddess Vṛṣādrīśvarī (his female counterpart). Is Lord Śrīnivāsa masculine or feminine for you?\n\nAvadhānī: He is Bālāji18.  \n\nPresident: If the concluding two lines of the Varṇanā are composed, then it will be complete.\n\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 18th time)\n\nAvadhānī: atulitabalavidyādharmarakṣaikadīkṣāḥ\n\nThe Bell: (sounds for the 19th time).\n\n(continues) iha sadasi sadasyāḥ paṇḍitāḥ me'tribhāgyāt//\n(Unequalled in power and knowledge, dedicated to the protection of Dharma, the scholars of this assembly (are present here) due to my good fortune.)\n\nNow the last Eshu?\n\n18In Hindi 'ji' is added at the end of a name as a sign of respect. 'Balaji' is another name of Lord Srinivasa of Tirupati. The Avadhānī splits the word Balaji into 'bala' and 'ji'. 'Bala' in Sanskrit is feminine meaning a girl. Thus the Avadhānī has solved the problem elegantly, with a pun and play of words.",
      "sanskritDevanagari": "सभापतिः:  समस्या: सम्पूणर्ा  ।   पुनः दत्तपद्याम् त`तीयः चतुथ्र्ाः ।\n\nअवधानी:  नूत्नाविष्व`ðतिकारिणी--- (घण्टा 17) नूत्नाविष्व`ðतिकारिणी सु#चिरा दिव्यज्जगन्मङ्गला                     \nप्रत्ना ते शुभमू£तर| हृदये धार्या वृषाद्रीश्वर ।।\n\nसभापतिः:  दत्तपद्याम् पादचतुÎयं सम्पू.र्ाम् ।   सम्प्रति व.र्ाने पाद};म् ।   त`तीयः पादः  चतुथ्र्ाः पादः ।\n\nव्यस्ताक्षरी:  }ादशमक्षरं क्ष\n\nअवधानी:  }ादशमक्षरं क्ष\n\nअपंस्तुतप्रसङ्गः  भोः अवधानिवर्य! वृषाद्रीश्वरं स्तुतवान् वा वृषाद्रीश्वर° स्तुतवान् वा ?       \nश्रीनिवासं वंð  कां वा मन्;ते भवान् ?\n\nअवधानी:  सा बायाजी\n\nसभापतिः:  व.र्ाने पाद}यं दी;ते त£ह अवधानम् सम्पूण± भविष्;ति ।                              (घण्टा 18)\n\nअवधानी: अतुलितबलविद्याधर्मरक्षैकदीक्षाः                                                     (घण्टा 19)\nइह सदसि सदस्याः पण्डिताः मेऽतिभाग्यात् ।।\n\nअन्ितमः आशुः ?"
