      "englishText": "Eshu: One hears much about a place called Konasiva, situated at quite a distance from your native place. When I remembered the Coconut trees, I had a desire to go there. Not only me but we all want to go there. Without delay, I request you now, to describe this place through words.\n\t\nPresident: However nowadays the Coconut trees have disappeared. Do you want him to describe the original spot or the place as it looks like today?\n\nAvadhānī: They are eager to see the place. So I will show them what is worth seeing.\n\nPresident: Then show the original scene.\n\nAvadhānī: (composes a verse in Mālinī— a fifteen-syllabled metre)\n   \t          \nsaphalabahulanārikelakelivilolāḥ\nvipulavividhasasyaśyāmalāsundarāṅgyaḥ/\namalapuratale yāḥ pūrvadṛśyāḥ \nThe Bell: (sounds for the 20th time)\n(continues) bhuvah tāḥ...\n\n(A site graced with many kinds of Coconut trees laden with fruit,swaying gently with widely stretching fields of various lavish crops,beautiful to watch. This pure place on Earth was Amalapura of olden days...)",
      "sanskritDevanagari": "आशुः  अत्रा भवतः आवासाद् अतिदूरे कोणसीव इति सुन्दरः प्रान्तः अस्ति इति Jू;ते। अत्रा नारिवेðयद्रुमाणांदश्र्ानेन तत्र गन्तुं आशा जनि ।  न वेðवयमहमधुना सवर्ेषां सवर्े वयं गन्तुकामाः ।  अनवकाशः अहं भवन्तं प्राथ्र्ाये वाग्व.र्ानेन नि#प;न्तु इति ।\n\nसभापतिः:  नारिवेðयद्रुमाः नÎाः सम्प्रति ।  किं मन्;ते ? प्रचीनद`श्यं मन्;ते अथवा आधुनिवंð द`श्;म् ?\n\nअवधानी:  द्रÎुमिच्छन्ित खलु ;द् दश्र्ानीयं तदेव दश्र्ायामि\n\nसभापतिः:  प्रचीनमेव दश्र्ा;तु\n\nअवधानी:  सफयबहुयनारिवेðयवेðयीविलोयः\n           विपुलविविधसस्;श्यामयासुन्दराङ्गîः ।                                               \n           अमयपुरतये याः पूर्वद`श्याः--- (घण्टा 20)                                                                                                              ---भुवः ताः---"
